<h2 id="what-qualifies-meaningful-stories" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. What qualifies (meaningful stories)</h2>

**Default: skip** only when the phase has **no durable lesson**. Completing an `aciub` / `implref` phase does **not** by itself require a new story—but a **good lesson is still a good lesson** even when similar code already shipped elsewhere.

Capture a story when **both** are true:

1. **Useful knowledge** — Non-trivial behavior of systems, frameworks, runtimes, data, security, cost, or reliability—not only “it broke once” with no mechanism.
2. **Reusable** — Helps **future work in this codebase** *or* could be told in a **senior / tech-lead interview** (tradeoffs, measurement, guardrails).

**Strong fits (examples):** **phased workflows** where each stage can use a different tool; dual or alternate backends; choices backed by **evaluation matrices**; orchestration; correctness under ambiguous inputs; operational safety (timeouts, idempotency). **Also counts:** deployment safety, recurring parser edge cases, cost/security implications, **developer speed** only when the lesson is **non-obvious**; **design strategy** choices (e.g. hybrid shared-helper + family allowlist vs one mega-prompt).

<table>
<thead>
<tr style="background:#1565c0;color:white"><th>Dimension</th><th>What it means</th><th>Skip war story?</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd"><b>A. Lesson already in <code>war_stories/</code></b></td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">Same reusable insight already has an index row (cite story <b>N</b>)</td><td style="background:#c8e6c9"><b>Yes — skip</b> (dedupe). Optional: one-line cross-link if this phase adds a new example.</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd"><b>B. Mechanism already in product code</b></td><td style="background:#fff3e0">e.g. “demos already do neighbor-fit” / pattern already implemented</td><td style="background:#ffcdd2"><b>No — not a skip reason by itself.</b> Code existence ≠ lesson captured. Write the story if the <b>insight</b> is not yet in the collection (or is a meaningfully sharper formulation).</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

**Forbidden skip excuses:** “mechanism already known from demos/scope X”; “we only swapped prompts”; “partial live win so nothing to teach”; “documented in the refactor plan / chat only.”

**Usually skip:** typos with no pattern; one-off mistakes with no lesson; “we shipped the plan checklist” **without a reusable insight**; pure CSS/chrome polish with no design trap; narratives that boil down to “we tried harder”; pure documentation formatting unless it encodes a **process** decision worth defending; **duplicates of an existing story-index row** (cite the row and skip — that is dimension **A** only).

**Technical vs design:** A candidate does **not** need to be a “classic bug” to qualify—clear **design** decisions ([§5.2](#design-decisions)) belong on equal footing with **implementation** lessons ([§5.1](#technical-lessons)) when they meet the bar above.

