<h2 id="story-kinds-technical-lessons-vs-design-decisions" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Story kinds: technical lessons vs design decisions</h2>

Neither kind is privileged for **`exwar`** extraction or hand authoring: **actively consider both** Tier-B-style technical incidents **and** Tier-A / design-heavy arcs—the curated **`WAR_STORIES_PORT_LEARN_SAMPLES.md`** blend is intentional ([§1.1](#purpose-audience-example)). When one story spans both, follow the **mixed-story** guidance in [§5.2](#design-decisions) for **`keywords:`**.

<h3 id="technical-lessons" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">5.1 Technical lessons</h3>

- **What:** Debugging outcomes, framework/runtime behavior, migrations, performance, tests, tooling—**how the system behaved** and what changed.
- **Keywords:** Concrete stack terms (`postgres`, `ffmpeg`, `openapi`, `jsonl`) plus the problem area. Include **`design`** only when the entry is also a design story.

<h3 id="design-decisions" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">5.2 Design decisions</h3>

- **What:** Choices among **alternatives** with consequences (data model, API shape, pipeline stages, UX rules, system boundaries).
- **Keywords (required):** the word **`design`** **and** a **second category** keyword, for example **`system design`**, **`API design`**, **`data model design`**, **`UX design`**.

If a story mixes bug fix and design, include **both** technical keywords and **`design` + category**.

**Design category keywords (searchable second term):**

| Second keyword (examples) | Use when the decision is mainly about… |
| --- | --- |
| **`system design`** | Platform / datastore / service boundaries, major stack fit |
| **`API design`** | Endpoints, contracts, optional fields, backward compatibility |
| **`data model design`** | Tables, keys, normalization, stat granularity |
| **`UX design`** | Interaction rules, affordances, visibility of feedback |

**Valid `keywords:` line examples (illustrative domains):**

- `keywords: design, system design, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, relational model, language learning`
- `keywords: design, API design, stat_person_codes, backward compatibility, FastAPI`
- `keywords: design, UX design, conjugation practice, double-click, submit gating`

**Technical lesson keyword flavor:** favor concrete stack words (`postgres`, `alembic`, `vite`, `cookie`, `react state`, `ffmpeg`, …) plus the problem area.

