<h2 id="entry-structure-and-metadata" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">8. Entry structure and metadata</h2>

Each story uses this layout.

- **Portable default:** Markdown **`## N. Short title`** and **`### N.m …`** subsections.
- **Repo override (common for colored previews):** HTML **`<h2>` / `<h3>`** using the **palette and `id` discipline** from **`.cursor/rules/mrkd-markdown-authoring.mdc`** §5. **Required when HTML is used for story titles:** stable anchors so outlines and in-file TOCs keep working—for example **`id="war-story-N"`** on the story title and **`id="war-story-N-sec-M"`** (or equivalent) on **Context / Root Cause / …** subsections. Subsection **labels** must stay **N.1–N.5** in visible text.

**Metadata** (plain lines immediately under the story title, before **N.1**):

- `**creation:** <YYMMDD-HHMMSS>` (or the timestamp style the collection already uses—stay consistent within the file)
- `**last_updated:** <YYMMDD-HHMMSS>`
- `**keywords:** ...` (comma-separated; grep-friendly)
- `**difficulty:** <1–10>` (how hard to find/fix or decide)
- `**significance:** <1–10>` (cost of repeating the mistake or wrong decision)

**Subsections** (same lesson structure every time):

- **`### N.1 Context`** — situation and goal  
- **`### N.2 Root Cause`** — mechanism / risk (**not** blame)  
- **`### N.3 Key Insight`** — memorable principle (optional short **highlight span**—see **`mrkd`** §7 restraint)  
- **`### N.4 Resolution`** — what we shipped or decided (use **tables / Mermaid** here when comparing options or phased pipelines—see [Visual aids](#visual-aids))  
- **`### N.5 Takeaway`** — one tight closing line

**While drafting:** collect commands, exit codes, config keys, file paths, and how the fix was **verified**.

- Optional: note **timezone** for timestamps in Context if it matters for the lesson.
- **Keywords** must keep **`grep`** useful—tools + problem area (e.g. `postgres, login, cookies`).

<h3 id="collection-file-scaffolding" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">8.1 Collection-level scaffolding (`WAR_STORIES.md`)</h3>

Large rolling collections (**many numbered stories**) should add **navigation and scan aids** near the **top** of **`war_stories/WAR_STORIES.md`**, aligned with **`mrkd`**:

1. **`Document outline`** — A first-class section (Markdown **`## Document outline`** or an **`<h2 id="document-outline">`** with the same role). Explain how stories are numbered and what **§N.1–N.5** mean so first-time readers are not lost.
2. **Reading guide table** — One compact **HTML table** (**`mrkd`** §6.1): columns such as **Field** / **Meaning** for metadata lines (**creation**, **keywords**, **difficulty**, …) and the five subsection names.
3. **Story index table** — **HTML table** listing **`#`** | linked **title** (anchor to **`#war-story-N`**) | **one-phrase gist**. Keeps dozens of arcs reachable without brute-force scrolling.
4. **On every append of story `N`** — Extend the story index row in the **same commit**; adjust intro copy only if filenames or rules drift.

When a repository provides reusable visual snippets under **`utils/styles/*`** (tables, Mermaid templates, badge palettes), **prefer those assets** for war-story visuals so `exwar` output stays consistent with project style packs. If **`utils/styles/*`** is absent, fallback to **`mrkd`** defaults (and keep any project-specific notes in **`war_stories/WAR_STORIES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC.md`**).

Minor collections (only a handful of stories) **may** skip the story index until growth makes it worthwhile—**do** still follow **`mrkd`** outline discipline once the file is multi-topic or long enough to scroll.

<h3 id="minimal-template" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">8.2 Minimal template (Markdown form)</h3>

```markdown
## N. Story title

**creation:** <YYMMDD-HHMMSS>
**last_updated:** <YYMMDD-HHMMSS>
**keywords:** keyword1, keyword2
**difficulty:** 1
**significance:** 1

### N.1 Context

### N.2 Root Cause

### N.3 Key Insight

### N.4 Resolution

### N.5 Takeaway
```

HTML collections: translate this skeleton into **`<h2 id="war-story-N">` / `<h3 id="war-story-N-sec-M">`** using **`mrkd`** §5 styling; keep the same **N.1–N.5** visible labels.

