<h2 id="visual-aids" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">11. Visual aids</h2>

- Default prose to **plain Markdown** paragraphs and short lists—**earn** visuals.
- Prefer **comparison tables**, **budget-split tables**, and **pipelined workflows** (**Mermaid**) in **§N.4 Resolution** whenever the arc has **explicit alternatives**, **multiple stages**, or **role boundaries** (e.g. local vs LLM, v1 vs v2). Dense design stories (**Tier A**, [§4](#tiering-arc-first-then-incidents)) should bias toward **`mrkd`** §6 visuals when they replace pages of narration.
- Follow **`.cursor/rules/mrkd-markdown-authoring.mdc`** **[section 6](#gma-visual-aids)** (HTML tables + Mermaid; keyword **`mrkd`**) as baseline. If **`utils/styles/*`** exists in this repo, `exwar` should actively reuse those visual aids whenever suitable (especially for Tier-A/system-design stories) rather than reinventing ad-hoc table/diagram styling.
- **`mrkd`** **§6 quick recall:** table headers **`background:#1565c0;color:white`**; optional **aspect** column **`#e3f2fd`**; alternating body tint rows (**`#e8f5e9`**, **`#fff3e0`**, **`#ffebee`** for risk paths); badges per **`mrkd`** §6.1.2 (**✓**, **⚠**, **recommended**, …). **Mermaid:** **`font-size:9px`** and consistent **`stroke-width:1px`** on `style` lines ([§6.2](#gma-mermaid)).
- Do **not** rely on **binary screenshots** as the main explanation unless the project explicitly standardizes on them (default: **no**).

**Inline badges (optional, use sparingly in story bodies):**

- <span style="background:#e3f2fd;padding:2px 4px">context</span>
- <span style="background:#fff3e0;padding:2px 4px">root cause</span>
- <span style="background:#e8f5e9;padding:2px 4px">resolution</span>
- <span style="background:#ffebee;padding:2px 4px">risk</span>

For **narrative rhythm** and **`mrkd`**-style tables/diagram density, skim **`.cursor/rules/war_stories_example/WAR_STORIES_PORT_LEARN_SAMPLES.md`** first, then **`WAR_STORIES_AWS.md`** (same folder) for longer-form pacing ([§1.1](#purpose-audience-example)).

