<h2 id="checklist-before-merge" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">13. Checklist before merge</h2>

- [ ] **Qualified** under [§3](#what-qualifies-meaningful-stories) — if not, **skip** (do not invent a story)
- [ ] **File choice** correct ([§2.1](#war-stories-directory-portable-convention)): portable → `WAR_STORIES.md`; product/ops/IA → `WAR_STORIES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC.md`
- [ ] **Assets:** any linked script or image lives under **`war_stories/assets/`** with **`assets/README.md`** updated
- [ ] Story number and **§N.1–§N.5** labels match anchor discipline (`###` headings **or** HTML **`h3`** with stable **`war-story-*`** ids)—see [§8](#entry-structure-and-metadata)
- [ ] Metadata lines present; timestamps plausible **and consistent** with the rest of the file
- [ ] At least one concrete detail (path, tool, version, endpoint, or number) in Context or Root Cause
- [ ] Code fences use correct language tags; technical lessons include **crucial** snippets with **English** inline comments when code teaches the lesson ([§10](#code-blocks))
- [ ] Each project **source** fence has **project name + repo-relative path**; GitHub link only if [§10.1](#code-source-attribution) stable—no broken URLs
- [ ] **`mrkd`**: outline + hierarchy + visual conventions—as applicable—for the **whole collection file**, not only the new story chunk
- [ ] Target file’s **story index** / outline updated in the same edit ([§8.1](#collection-file-scaffolding))
- [ ] **Tier A / design** arcs: **`§N.4`** used comparison or pipeline visuals when prose alone buried the takeaway?
- [ ] No **exclusive** reliance on ephemeral paths (**`cursor_gen/`**, unpublished plans)—essential decision content **copied inline** (`§N.4`)
- [ ] Final story text does **not** explicitly reference `cursor_gen/*` paths (content absorbed into durable sections instead)
- [ ] Tables / Mermaid **only** where helpful; if used, prefer reusable visuals from **`utils/styles/*`** when present, else follow **`mrkd`** **[§6](#gma-visual-aids)** (colors, typography, badges)
- [ ] Language is **easy to scan**; acronyms and jargon limited or explained **once**
- [ ] For **design** stories, **keywords** include **`design`** and a **category** keyword (see [Story kinds](#story-kinds-technical-lessons-vs-design-decisions))
- [ ] **Exemplars:** Checked structure and visuals against **`.cursor/rules/war_stories_example/WAR_STORIES_PORT_LEARN_SAMPLES.md`** (**primary**) and **`WAR_STORIES_AWS.md`** when extra density helps ([§1.1](#purpose-audience-example))
- [ ] **Voice:** No literal **`interview`** (or "demonstrates my skill" / "classic X question" / "sound bite") inside **`N.1`**–**`N.5`** prose or **`keywords:`**; no first-person "I" narration ([§1.2](#voice-and-register))

<h2 id="cursor-behavior" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">14. Cursor behavior</h2>

- **`alwaysApply: false`** — remains **off** globally. This rule enters context when the user **@**-mentions **`exwar-war-stories-extraction`**, includes **`exwar`** in the prompt, or edits paths matched by **`globs`** (**`war_stories/`**, **`war_stories_example/`** rule bundle).
- When proposing or drafting stories, **`exwar`** should **consult both** **`.cursor/rules/war_stories_example/WAR_STORIES_PORT_LEARN_SAMPLES.md`** (**primary**) and **`WAR_STORIES_AWS.md`** in that folder (**secondary**) for structure and visuals—without treating either as the live collection ([§1.1](#purpose-audience-example)).
- Extraction still needs a **qualifying** conversation or an explicit **exwar** / user request (e.g. “extract war stories from the last thread”).
- If the user wants depth on **this** rule’s structure, point them to **this file**—do not defer to external repos.
- `exwar` output is considered incomplete unless visual aids are applied appropriately: **use `utils/styles/*` artifacts when available**, otherwise satisfy **`mrkd-markdown-authoring.mdc`** checks (see [Checklist before merge](#checklist-before-merge)).

