<h2 id="session-trigger-exwar-duration" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">15. Session trigger `exwar [duration]`</h2>

When the user’s prompt contains **`exwar`** as a **standalone token** (whole word), treat it as an instruction to **extract new war stories from this same Cursor chat session**, scoped by time **backward from when the user sent the prompt**.

**Syntax**

| Form | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| **`exwar`** | Review discussion in this chat within the **default lookback: 24 hours** (intent scope). |
| **`exwar <n>h`** | **`n`** positive integer — lookback **n hours** (e.g. `exwar 4h` → last **4 hours**). |
| **`exwar <n>d`** | lookback **n days** (e.g. `exwar 4d`). |
| **`exwar <n>w`** | lookback **n weeks** (e.g. `exwar 4w`). |

Whitespace between **`exwar`** and the duration is allowed (e.g. `exwar 4h`, `exwar  4d`). Unsupported suffixes → ask for clarification or fall back to **`exwar`** default.

**Chat history (what you can read):** For **`exwar`**, **assume this Cursor chat’s thread is readable** for every **user** and **assistant** message the host has **included in the current agent context** for this request. That is the working transcript: **use it** to find new stories. The duration token (**`4h`**, **`4d`**, etc.) is a **relevance / recency filter** for what to emphasize (and a user intent for “how far back to care”); you usually **do not** have reliable per-message wall-clock times in the raw context—treat “last 4 hours” as **recent turns at the end of the visible thread**, not as a server-side query.

**Behavior**

1. **Read** **`war_stories/WAR_STORIES.md`** (and companion **`war_stories/WAR_STORIES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC.md`** if present) so new entries **do not duplicate** stories already captured—focus on **meaningfully different** lessons ([What qualifies](#what-qualifies-meaningful-stories), [Tiering](#tiering-arc-first-then-incidents)).
2. **Review** this conversation (as visible in context) for material **matching the declared lookback intent**—prioritize **arc-level** and **high-signal** incidents before noise ([Workflow: batch](#workflow-batch-from-chat-history)).
3. **Draft** ranked candidates, then **append** new numbered stories per [Entry structure and metadata](#entry-structure-and-metadata); apply [Readability](#readability-and-markdown-authoring) (**`mrkd`** / **`mrkd-markdown-authoring.mdc`**). **Maintain** [Collection scaffolding](#collection-file-scaffolding) (story index / outline) when that file already uses it. **Before finalizing**, skim **both** **`.cursor/rules/war_stories_example/`** exemplars—**`WAR_STORIES_PORT_LEARN_SAMPLES.md`** first—for structure, keyword mix, and visuals ([§1.1](#purpose-audience-example)).

**Context window limit:** Long threads may be **truncated, summarized, or compacted** by the IDE—then early turns might be **missing** even if **`exwar 4w`** was asked. If the requested span **likely exceeds** what is visible, **say so**, work from **visible** turns only, or ask the user to **paste** missing parts / export—do **not** invent missing discussion.

